<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HUMAN GOLD RUSH LESSON</p><h1>The Tiger’s Eye Covenant</h1><p class="intro">A touchstone held in the hand can create a pause long enough to choose how we meet another person.</p><blockquote>What changes when we carry our values in the palm of our hand?</blockquote><div class="actions"><a href="prepare-laugh-event.html">Take the Covenant, Receive Your Stone<span>→</span></a></div><aside class="notice"><strong>A modern-day pet rock</strong><p>The Tiger’s Eye touchstone borrows the pet-rock premise on purpose — a plain object made meaningful by a story and a ritual, not by its shape.</p></aside></header><section class="content-grid"><article><span>01</span><div><h2>Practice, not perfection</h2><p>FAITH means Fair, Accepting, Insightful, Transparent, and Humble. The covenant asks for practice rather than agreement, conformity, or perfection.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h2>A physical reminder</h2><p>The Tiger’s Eye touchstone is not money, a ticket, or proof of virtue. It is a personal prompt to bring the covenant into everyday relationships.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h2>Gather</h2><p>Picking up your touchstone is simply a fulfillment center activity — no public pledge, no demonstration, no audience. Take the covenant privately, in your own time, and carry it home.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h2>Notice</h2><p>Notice whether a physical reminder changes the pause between feeling and action. Never grade another person’s sincerity.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h2>Two tumbled gemstones</h2><p>A single lapidary pilot in Dahlonega, Georgia produces two different touchstones used in this study — the Tiger’s Eye covenant stone described on this page, and a second, separate tumbled gemstone for YAM’ers. Postcards, not ads, direct people to RSVP and pick one up at a local LAUGH fulfillment center — you are scheduled for pickup, not received by accident.</p></div></article><article><span>06</span><div><h2>A YAM’er’s pickup</h2><p>A YAM’er who takes the covenant to practice FAITH is simply notified when and where to pick up their tumbled gemstone at a local LAUGH event — triggered by selecting a Peace Pentagon branch to support. This second stone is a different gemstone, not shaped like a worry/prayer stone and not the Tiger’s Eye itself.</p></div></article></section><section class="media-section"><div class="section-heading"><p>MEDIA FOR THIS LESSON</p><h2>Watch, listen, and discuss</h2></div><div class="media-grid"><article class="media-card video"><div class="media-frame"><span>▶</span><small>VIDEO 1</small></div><h3>The Tiger’s Eye Covenant: orientation</h3><p>Reserved for the featured story or introductory video.</p><a href="#">Transcript coming soon</a></article><article class="media-card video"><div class="media-frame"><span>▶</span><small>VIDEO 2</small></div><h3>Community conversation</h3><p>Reserved for a demonstration, conversation, or local example.</p><a href="#">Discussion guide coming soon</a></article><article class="media-card podcast"><div class="media-frame"><span>◉</span><small>PODCAST</small></div><h3>Listen and reflect</h3><p>Reserved for the facilitator or community podcast episode.</p><a href="#">Transcript coming soon</a></article></div></section>